tion $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(-3,-1),(-4,0),(-2,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/assets/548c907226db9cbdc8fb4dd18c74f3a2001ba7d90973c6f433f67b3e6b87fd29.png)"}]}
